Verification Reference

Verification Objective

Demonstrate that the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) can interpret relevant observations and establish an operational context in accordance with the requirements of SO-F-003.

---

Verification Method

Verification shall be achieved through one or more of the following methods:

Method| Purpose
Analysis| Confirm that the interpretation architecture can transform relevant observations into an operational context.
Demonstration| Show that the system establishes appropriate context from representative observation sets.
Test| Evaluate contextual interpretation across defined operating scenarios, including changing and uncertain conditions.

---

Verification Reference

Detailed verification procedures, test cases, datasets, and evidence shall be maintained within the AVIA Verification domain and referenced from this objective upon approval.

---

Verification Success Criteria

Verification shall demonstrate that the system can:

- Establish meaningful relationships among relevant observations.
- Determine the operational significance of observed conditions.
- Produce an interpretable operating context.
- Update the operating context when relevant observations change.
- Represent interpretation confidence or uncertainty where required.
- Provide contextual information suitable for downstream decision generation.

---

Verification Boundary

Verification of SO-F-003 shall evaluate the interpretation capability independently of final action selection and execution.

The verification shall not establish whether a subsequent decision is correct or whether an approved action is successfully executed. Those capabilities shall be evaluated under their respective objectives.

---

